From 31c202dade9ac4aac48644752a273ca7ec55d3e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:14:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/29] fix(task35): re-freeze the 176/175-program historical
 projection hashes for 0ed489ec

test_current_and_task35_absent_generation_are_exact_and_isolated
regenerates two historical typed-slice projections (the 176-program
Task-35/Grain-175 boundary, and that set minus synth/bitwise:bitwise
itself) and compares them to frozen shas. Three of its four frozen
values had gone stale under the 0ed489ec corpus bump.

Audit (rule 2, done in place of reconstruction_audit.py since no old/new
regen-cache pair exists for this pin -- see method below):

1. Diffed the two corpus source trees directly (a024dc3a vs 0ed489ec):
   exactly 17 files differ, matching intended change (f).
2. Cross-referenced those 17 program keys against this test's own
   exclusion set (the historical milestone's fixed removal list, read
   from the test itself). 10 of the 17 changed programs are NOT excluded
   and so are part of both the 176- and 175-program projections:
   filter/adjust:adjust, filter/chrome:chMap, filter/grade:primary,
   filter/grade:vignette, filter/invert:inv, filter/text:text,
   filter/tint:colorize, mixer/alphaMask:alphaMask,
   mixer/blendMode:blendMode, synth/media:mediaInput.
3. Regenerated both projections from the live tree (same
   generate_outputs/historical_cross_lane call path the test itself
   uses) and confirmed: the isolated synth/bitwise:bitwise block hash is
   UNCHANGED (bitwise's own corpus source isn't one of the 17 -- this
   assertion was already passing), while the three aggregate/whole-file
   hashes that span the other 175 programs are exactly the three that
   were stale. No other difference exists between the frozen and live
   projections; the drift is fully accounted for by the 10 included
   changed programs.

Re-pinned all three: the 175-program aggregate block hash, and the
without-task35 175-program projection's typed_slice.cpp and
typed_manifest.json whole-file hashes. All 4 tests in the module now
pass (Ran 4 tests ... OK).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EU6jaFnvpzrcsgg8pXrwK2
